🚀 Java 8 Programming Interview Questions (Text Format)
Fast Revision | Question → Input → Code → Output

1. Filter Even Numbers
Input: [1,2,3,4,5,6]
Code:
list.stream()
    .filter(n -> n % 2 == 0)
    .toList();
Output: [2,4,6]

2. Filter Odd Numbers
Input: [1,2,3,4,5,6]
Code:
list.stream()
    .filter(n -> n % 2 != 0)
    .toList();
Output: [1,3,5]

3. Convert To Uppercase
Input: [java,spring,kafka]
Code:
names.stream()
     .map(String::toUpperCase)
     .toList();
Output: [JAVA,SPRING,KAFKA]

4. Convert To Lowercase
Input: [JAVA,SPRING,KAFKA]
Code:
names.stream()
     .map(String::toLowerCase)
     .toList();
Output: [java,spring,kafka]

5. Sum Of Numbers
Input: [10,20,30,40]
Code:
list.stream()
    .mapToInt(Integer::intValue)
    .sum();
Output: 100

6. Average Of Numbers
Input: [10,20,30,40]
Code:
list.stream()
    .mapToInt(Integer::intValue)
    .average();
Output: OptionalDouble[25.0]

7. Maximum Number
Input: [5,8,2,12,3]
Code:
list.stream().max(Integer::compareTo).get();
Output: 12

8. Minimum Number
Input: [5,8,2,12,3]
Code:
list.stream().min(Integer::compareTo).get();
Output: 2

9. Count Elements
Input: [10,20,30,40,50]
Code:
list.stream().count();
Output: 5

10. Remove Duplicates
Input: [1,2,2,3,3,4,5]
Code:
list.stream().distinct().toList();
Output: [1,2,3,4,5]

11. Sort Ascending
Input: [8,3,1,6,2]
Code:
list.stream().sorted().toList();
Output: [1,2,3,6,8]

12. Sort Descending
Input: [8,3,1,6,2]
Code:
list.stream().sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder()).toList();
Output: [8,6,3,2,1]

13. Get First Element
Input: [100,200,300]
Code:
list.stream().findFirst().get();
Output: 100

14. Check Any Match
Input: [10,20,70,80]
Code:
list.stream().anyMatch(n -> n > 50);
Output: true

15. Check All Match
Input: [10,20,30]
Code:
list.stream().allMatch(n -> n > 0);
Output: true

16. Check None Match
Input: [10,20,30]
Code:
list.stream().noneMatch(n -> n < 0);
Output: true

17. Skip First 2 Elements
Input: [10,20,30,40,50]
Code:
list.stream().skip(2).toList();
Output: [30,40,50]

18. Get First 3 Elements
Input: [10,20,30,40,50]
Code:
list.stream().limit(3).toList();
Output: [10,20,30]

19. Sort String By Length
Input: [Spring,Java,Microservices]
Code:
names.stream().sorted(Comparator.comparing(String::length)).toList();
Output: [Java,Spring,Microservices]

20. Join Strings
Input: [Java,Spring,Kafka]
Code:
names.stream().collect(Collectors.joining(","));
Output: Java,Spring,Kafka
